      "content": "Hello! In structural analysis, live load refers to the temporary forces acting on the deck, such as people, furniture, and vehicles, while dead load includes the permanent forces from the weight of the structure itself, like the deck's own weight and any permanent fixtures. Remember to account for both loads in your beam calculations to comply with VPDCD guidelines and ensure the safety and durability of your cantilever deck. Good luck with your project, and I hope everything clears permit approval smoothly! If you need further assistance, don't hesitate to ask.",
